parts.text:
The dye trade deliberately ripens everything in sunlight, so a Tyrian dyer handles purple all day without effect. The guild works the other way:
- it processes in lamplit, windowless vault-workshops;
- it seals the liquor in closed jars, the vessel type found at Kolonna [2];
- it stores it dried to powder in the dark [4].
The three species give different 'shades' of potency [1, 16]. As a proposal, banded-murex liquor, which in reality ripens without light [5], is unstable and hard to keep potent, while spiny-murex liquor keeps best in the dark. That would make the spiny murex the guild's prize.
